- Kill the supervisor process (independent_supervisor_100.sh loop): that's a global infrastructure action, not a bounded worker action. The previous worker flagged it. But it's arguably the root cause of burning budget across all 100 workers. Hmm. The user (human PI) would probably want the loop stopped, but a bounded worker should not unilaterally kill the swarm supervisor — that could be considered destructive and beyond authority. Also, the sandbox may or may not allow killing processes. I should not do that.
